{{High Risk|Template:Completion request|nocat=1|pagetype=Main}}
Displays a "Completion Requested" notice box and files the page into [[:Category:Completion Requests]], marking an article that is missing substantial information. Use it to invite editors to expand a page — for a page actively being reworked, use {{T|Maintenance}} instead.

Categorization applies on '''article''' and '''category''' pages only; it is skipped in other namespaces, so the template is safe to demonstrate in documentation.

==Syntax==
{{T|Completion request|block=1
|v1=noun
|v2=info =
}}

==Examples==
===Default===
{{T|Completion request|_Y_=1}}

===Naming what is incomplete===
The first positional parameter fills in the noun in the default sentence.
{{T|Completion request|_Y_=1|p1=section}}

===Custom message===
<code>info</code> replaces the default sentence entirely and takes precedence over the positional parameter.
{{T|Completion request|_Y_=1|p1=info = This discography is missing releases from 2019 onward.}}

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>1</code> || – || Content type || The noun used in the default message, as in "This ''section'' is incomplete." Ignored when <code>info</code> is set. || string || article ||
|-
| <code>info</code> || – || Custom message || A full replacement for the default message. Overrides parameter 1. || string || – ||
|}

